# text = And now behold, this was the desire which I desired of him-- that if it should so be that my people, the Nephites, should fall into transgression, and by any means be destroyed, and the Lamanites should not be destroyed, that the Lord God would preserve a record of my people, the Nephites; even if it so be by the power of his holy arm, that it might be brought forth at some future day unto the Lamanites, that, perhaps, they might be brought unto salvation--
# sent_id = 14
# llm_note = Very long sentence. "this was the desire" is root copular clause. "which I desired of him" is acl:relcl on "desire". "that if it should so be..." is the content of the desire (ccomp/appositive of "desire"). The nested conditional structure: "if it should so be that my people should fall... and be destroyed, and the Lamanites should not be destroyed, that the Lord God would preserve a record". "even if it so be by the power..." is a second conditional extending the wish. "that, perhaps, they might be brought unto salvation" is purpose/result clause. "the Nephites" (tok 26) is appositive to "my people" (tok 23). Second "the Nephites" (tok 61) is appositive to second "my people" (tok 58). "Lord God" is a compound PROPN.
